{
  "quest.3C0D9DFFEC915E2C.quest_subtitle": "Transfers Fluids",
  "quest.67E799DBD2A9F83C.quest_desc": [
    "Module filter slots take more than plain items. These filter items match whole groups at once:",
    "",
    "- &aTag Filter&r: matches items by item tag, such as every ore or every log.",
    "- &2Mod Filter&r: matches everything from one mod.",
    "[\"\", \"- \", {\"text\": \"Regex Filter\", \"color\": \"green\"}, \": matches registry names against a pattern. Press \", {\"keybind\": \"key.debug.modifier\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: F3\"}}, \"+\", {\"keybind\": \"key.debug.showAdvancedTooltips\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: H\"}}, \" to see those names on tooltips.\"]",
    "- &2Inspection Filter&r: checks durability, enchantments, food value, stored energy or fluid level.",
    "- &aBulk Item Filter&r: holds a long item list. Sneak + Right-click an inventory with it to add everything inside.",
    "",
    "Right-click a filter in the air to set it up, then put it in a module's filter slots like any other item.",
  ],
  "quest.75C48C2336AC44FE.quest_desc": [
    "With a &aPlayer Module&r, the &dRouter&r moves items straight to or from a player's inventory from anywhere, as long as that player is online. Sneak + Right-click a block with the module to make yourself its owner.",
    "",
    "The module screen sets the direction and which part of the inventory it uses. The choices are the main inventory with or without the hotbar, the armor slots, the offhand slot and your ender chest.",
    "",
    "Fill the &dRouter&r from a chest of food or ammo and set the module to send to you. Your supply then refills itself while you explore.",
  ],
  "quest.64E34B2DA32D3586.quest_desc": [
    "In this &bChapter&r, you'll find most of the ways to handle transferring items, energy, fluids, and more!",
  ],
  "task.56AEAE6BD791EA6C.title": "&fEnergy Cables",
  "quest.5778BAEC8F095B3D.title": "&eLaserIO",
  "quest.263A989631CE6F13.quest_desc": [
    "Every &aCrafting Storage&r and &aCo-Processor&r in a &eNodeworks&r CPU makes &bheat&r, and more of it when packed against other CPU parts. When your coolant can't keep up, the CPU slows down.",
    "",
    "&aCoolants&r count as part of the CPU, so you can use them to link parts together. ",
    "Any coolant touching a CPU block cools it, and each one gets a &bcluster bonus&r for every other coolant next to it. A solid wall of coolant works far better than single blocks spread around.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "&aCrafting Coolant&r: 1 cooling, +1 per neighboring coolant",
    "",
    "&3Adamantite Coolant&r: 2 cooling, +2 per neighboring coolant",
    "",
    "&dAeternium Coolant&r: 3 cooling, +3 per neighboring coolant",
    "",
    "&6Aurichalcum Coolant&r: 4 cooling, +4 per neighboring coolant",
    "",
    "A single layer of &3Adamantite Coolant&r against your CPU is enough to fully cool any part of it. Higher tiers do the same job with fewer blocks.",
  ],
  "quest.366F506F69C65F28.quest_desc": [
    "An &aItem Conduit&r extracts and inserts on its own, with no external pipe needed.",
    "",
    "Each connection gets its own filter and round-robin setting, so one conduit can pull from a furnace bank and split the output three ways without a second block.",
    "",
    "A &aConduit Probe&r copies a connection's settings, which saves configuring twenty identical faces by hand.",
  ],
  "quest.094A066E08994C5B.title": "&5Autocrafting",
  "quest.2F608401E82C349F.title": "&6Disks and Tools",
  "quest.5CA5F9BE51C24FC8.title": "&fRedstone Card",
  "quest.1AE69DDE0FBE9E9F.title": "&fItem Pipe",
  "quest.70A9E1AC900A77B4.quest_desc": [
    "&aPlayer Transmitters&r are used to power items in your inventory.",
    "",
    "To do this, you'll need to first make a &aBinding Card&r, then use it in your hand to claim it. Placing the card in the Transmitter will tell it to power your inventory.",
    "",
    "You can also use the &aBinding Card&r on an Enderman to convert it into a &dDimensional Binding Card&r, which allows the Transmitter to work across dimensions.",
  ],
  "quest.6A4A2A2EFD552316.quest_desc": [
    "If you're looking to store your power, &aEnergy Cells&r will do the trick.",
    "",
    "You can also craft &aBatteries&r and charge them up using the Cells. The Batteries can then be used to charge items in your inventory in the early game!",
  ],
  "quest.1CFBFD1CE648772F.title": "&5Ender &rCells",
  "quest.4348D85E3DB176E2.quest_desc": [
    "To allow a &dRouter&r to handle power, you'll need to give it &aEnergy Upgrades&r.",
    "",
    "Each upgrade increases its &bTotal Energy Buffer&r, as well as the total &bEnergy Transfer Rate&r per operation. These upgrades stack up to a max of 64.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "To transfer power out, you can use the &aEnergy Output Module&r. Holding this module then using it allows you to configure which face you'd like to output energy from in the &dRouter&r.",
    "",
    "To distribute power wirelessly, use the &6Energy Distributor Module&r. Sneak-using this module on a block adds it to the list of blocks to send power to, up to a certain range from the &dRouter&r.",
    "",
    "You can increase the range using &aRange Up Augments&r inside of the module itself.",
  ],
  "quest.5CA9AE56F2504859.title": "&fDropping and Voiding",
  "quest.40255F6F1C60B588.title": "&fFluid Interfaces",
  "quest.623C567053E87FA7.quest_desc": [
    "A &aBroadcast Antenna&r shares part of a network without a pipe. What it shares depends on the block it sits on top of.",
    "",
    "- &aNetwork Controller&r: a &2Portable Inventory Terminal&r can reach the network from anywhere in range.",
    "- &aProcessing Storage&r: another network can use its Processing Sets for autocrafting.",
    "- &aExport Chest&r: items pushed into the chest go straight to a paired &2Receiver Antenna&r sitting on an Import Chest.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Pairing uses a &aLink Crystal&r. Put it in the Broadcast Antenna's top slot and take it back out, then slot it into the Receiver Antenna or the Portable Inventory Terminal.",
    "",
    "Range is 128 blocks. The &dDimension Range Upgrade&r extends it to the whole dimension the antenna is in, and the &5Multi-Dimension Range Upgrade&r reaches every dimension.",
  ],
  "quest.606A9E518DA6CAE5.quest_desc": [
    "&eEntangled&r allows you to bind two blocks together, allowing you to interact with them as if they were the same block!",
    "",
    "This allows you to transfer items, energy, fluids, and more instantly. ",
    "",
    "&7&oUseful for hiding your messy cables.&r",
  ],
  "quest.2E2B7F19B5EF8240.quest_desc": [
    "The &aPlacer Module&r places the item in the buffer as a block, in the module's chosen direction.",
    "",
    "&aExtruder Modules&r build a whole line. By default the &aExtruder Module Mk1&r places blocks from the buffer while the &dRouter&r has a redstone signal, reaching 16 blocks out (32 with &2Range Up Augments&r). Cut the signal and it breaks them back into the buffer, so it makes a good retractable bridge or door.",
    "",
    "The &dExtruder Module Mk2&r reaches 32 blocks (64 with augments) and places template blocks copied from its own template slots. Templates can't be mined for drops, so the Mk2 never uses up real blocks.",
  ],
  "quest.2A65FC21A4BBF686.title": "&fEnergy Pipe",
  "quest.366F506F69C65F28.quest_subtitle": "Transfers Items",
  "quest.7E0E540CF7DB9A40.title": "&6Printing Press",
  "task.5B0B7A1B78FA15B6.title": "&fEnergy Cells",
  "quest.718AF92800C06825.quest_desc": [
    "If you've ever wanted to filter out which mobs that spawn within a certain area, the &aInterdiction Pylon&r is the machine for the job.",
    "",
    "This &aPylon&r uses &2Mob Filters&r to configure which mobs spawn within its radius. To filter out which mobs can spawn, craft a Mob Filter and use it on the mob you want to stop spawning.",
    "",
    "While it has niche uses, this could be great to use for creating specific natural mob farms like a Wither Skeleton farm in a Nether Fortress.",
  ],
  "quest.571145179B74FD13.quest_desc": [
    "The &dNetwork Controller&r anchors the whole network. &aNodes&r extend it outward, and &2Device Frames&r hold the machinery you attach to it.",
    "",
    "Start with the &bNodeworks Book&r; right-click it for the in-game guide, which covers considerably more than a quest chapter reasonably can.",
    "",
    "&7&oThe Network Wrench and Diagnostic Tool are what you'll use to build and debug it.&r",
  ],
  "task.55F5BD3470BD58A4.title": "Energizing Rods",
  "quest.606A9E518DA6CAE5.title": "&eEntangled Blocks",
  "quest.1A95C1F8C74D759C.title": "&dCrossing Dimensions",
  "quest.2E2B7F19B5EF8240.title": "&fPlacing Blocks",
  "quest.0DB5CBE2E76D2FD9.quest_desc": [
    "If you're looking for a pipe to transfer pretty much anything in or out, the &ePipez&r mod has you covered.",
    "",
    "Use its pipes to transfer &bitems&r, &9fluids&r and &cpower&r. &2Universal Pipes&r combine these in one pipe.",
    "",
    "Sneak + Right-click the end connected to your source with any compatible &aWrench&r to enable extraction. Add a &2Pipe Upgrade&r for faster transfer and filtering options.",
  ],
  "quest.0ED940DF43A934ED.title": "&fVacuum Module",
  "quest.38869642A2E6F8B6.title": "&eModular Routers",
  "quest.3C0D9DFFEC915E2C.quest_desc": [
    "Liquids move through the same bundle as everything else once you add a &aFluid Conduit&r.",
    "",
    "Its tooltip quotes two numbers. &bRate&r is per network tick, &bEffective Rate&r is what you actually get per tick once the network tick rate is applied, and the second one is the number to plan around.",
  ],
  "quest.1CFBFD1CE648772F.quest_desc": [
    "If you want to tap into your power storage wirelessly, you should pump your power into an &dEnder Cell&r.",
    "",
    "These are used to store a massive amount of power into a &bfrequency&r, which can be accessed from any dimension using another Ender Cell or &6Ender Gate&r.",
  ],
  "quest.38869642A2E6F8B6.quest_desc": [
    "When it comes to logistics, &eModular Routers&r can do it all. This mod comes with tons of useful features, like &aAuto-Clicking&r, &2Block Breaking&r, and more!",
    "",
    "All of these features are done within the main block, the &dModular Router&r. To give it a function, it needs a &aModule&r to tell it what to do. These Modules can be configured and upgraded using &aAugments&r.",
    "",
    "The &dRouter&r itself can also be upgraded in many different ways using &aUpgrades&r, which determine how it uses the Modules placed inside.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "By default, &dRouters&r come with a single item slot buffer. This can hold up to a stack of a single item.",
    "",
    "You can upgrade the &dRouter&r to handle other things like &9Fluids&r or &cPower&r using specific upgrades and modules.",
  ],
  "quest.1F2E5FBD59466D57.title": "&fWorking With Fluids",
  "quest.2DA8D6D984D83AC5.quest_desc": [
    "A &aSecurity Upgrade&r limits the &dRouter&r to you and the players listed on it. Right-click a player with the upgrade to add them, and Sneak + Right-click to remove them.",
    "",
    "It also makes several modules act as you, which helps when chunk claims would otherwise block them. Your own &aActivator Module&r can't attack you either.",
    "",
    "The &aCamouflage Upgrade&r makes the &dRouter&r look like another block. Sneak + Right-click a solid block with it to copy that block's look.",
  ],
  "quest.2F608401E82C349F.quest_desc": [
    "The &aNetwork Tool&r shows you what a manager can currently see, which is the fastest way to work out why a program isn't doing anything.",
    "",
    "&aProgram Disks&r save a script so you can carry it to another manager or hand it to someone else.",
  ],
  "quest.2A1AE478A678C1A9.title": "&fEnergy Interfaces",
  "quest.1F6FE0AAF690665D.quest_desc": [
    "You can make several &bRouter Upgrades&r that can help make your automation setups run better.",
    "",
    "The &aSpeed Upgrade&r increases how fast the &dRouter&r executes the installed modules.",
    "",
    "The &aStack Upgrade&r allows the &dRouter&r to interact with stacks of items at a time, rather than a single item.",
    "",
    "To upgrade Modules, you'll need to use &aAugments&r instead of upgrades.",
  ],
  "task.096452CE0C4FC543.title": "Any Hoe",
  "quest.5CA9AE56F2504859.quest_desc": [
    "Not every item needs a chest. The &aDropper Module&r drops items from the buffer in the module's chosen direction, and the &2Flinger Module&r throws them much farther. Set the Flinger's speed, pitch and yaw in its screen.",
    "",
    "The &aVoid Module&r destroys anything that reaches the buffer. With a &aVacuum Module&r and a filter in the same &dRouter&r, it clears junk drops out of a mob farm.",
    "",
    "&cItems sent into a Void Module are gone for good, so set its filter before you put it in the router.",
  ],
  "quest.745140E3D92CB0D6.title": "&fBlock Breaking",
  "quest.4F092D86017F37E9.title": "&fEnergizing Orb",
  "quest.67E799DBD2A9F83C.title": "&fSmarter Filters",
  "quest.64E34B2DA32D3586.title": "&fGeneral Logistics",
  "quest.718AF92800C06825.title": "&fInterdiction Pylon",
  "quest.314E9901D4E89E6F.title": "&fRedstone Detection",
  "quest.7384B838D821EDFC.quest_desc": [
    "A &aTurtle&r is a computer that can move, mine, build and interact with the world. Give it a program and it will go and do the job on its own.",
    "",
    "&aWired Modems&r and &2Networking Cable&r link computers to each other and to peripherals; Wireless and Ender Modems do the same without the cable, the latter across dimensions.",
    "",
    "&7&oA mining turtle running a quarry program is the classic first project.&r",
  ],
  "quest.258F5FED2D319C15.quest_desc": [
    "Nodeworks reaches into the world as well as into chests.",
    "",
    "- &aPlacer&r puts blocks down. &bBreaker&r takes them back up. &3User&r operates items on the world for you.",
    "- &2Variable&r stores a value the rest of the network can read.",
    "- &aScripting Terminal&r is where it stops being a storage mod and starts being a programmable one.",
    "",
    "&7&oThis is the deep end. The Nodeworks Book covers scripting properly.&r",
  ],
  "quest.1F2E5FBD59466D57.quest_desc": [
    "The &aFluid Module&r allows the &dRouter&r to handle fluids, as long as it has some kind of storage item in the buffer like a &2Bucket&r or a Tank.",
    "",
    "The &aFluid Module Mk.1&r allows the router to interact with any adjacent blocks, which can be set in the module interface.",
    "",
    "The &aFluid Module Mk.2&r allows for wireless transfer of fluids, and works just like the distributor modules for items.",
    "",
    "To upgrade the transfer rate of fluids, you can install &aFluid Transfer Upgrades&r into the &dRouter&r. &aSpeed Upgrades&r will determine how often it pulls or pushes fluids, and can be great to install as well.",
  ],
  "quest.4F092D86017F37E9.quest_desc": [
    "We can make some of the basics using Iron, but to improve our setup we'll need to make some stronger alloys by using the &aEnergizing Orb&r.",
    "",
    "To use this, you'll need power going into &bEnergizing Rods&r within 4 blocks of the Orb. When given the right items, the Rods will send power into the &aOrb&r to energize the items.",
    "",
    "The Energizing Orb is how you create the different tiers of items in the mod. &bBasic Energizing Rods&r will struggle to make the higher tier materials like &bNiotic Crystals&r, so upgrading those is a must as you progress!",
  ],
  "quest.4BBEE37F0D847BA9.quest_desc": [
    "&aFluid Pipes&r are the same idea for liquids, wrench and all.",
    "",
    "Bare pipe carries 50 mB/t. With an &aUltimate Pipe Upgrade&r that becomes 10,000 mB/t, which is enough for anything short of a large reactor loop.",
  ],
  "quest.0DB5CBE2E76D2FD9.title": "&ePipez",
  "quest.1DAA004E88230E24.quest_desc": [
    "You do not craft filters in this version. Each channel has its own grid of six filter slots on the right of the node's settings screen. Left-click an empty slot and pick one of three types.",
    "",
    "- &aNormal&r: up to 45 items, fluids or tags, each with its own rules for NBT, durability, slots and stock.",
    "- &aMod&r: everything from one mod ID.",
    "- &aRegex&r: matches display names against a limited regex pattern.",
    "",
    "Any filter can be a whitelist or a blacklist. The &bAny&r and &bAll&r toggle above the grid decides whether a resource has to pass one filter or every filter in the grid.",
    "",
    "&bStock&r means something different on each side. On a Sender it is the reserve left behind in the source. On a Receiver it is the most the destination is allowed to hold.",
  ],
  "quest.366F506F69C65F28.title": "&fItem Conduit",
  "quest.799515068A0B6D57.title": "&fAuto-Clicking",
  "quest.7F4E7C687E7D8707.quest_desc": [
    "The &aBasic Item Collector&r is a configurable collector that automatically collects items within its radius and pushes them into an inventory below.",
    "",
    "By default, the &aBasic Item Collector&r can collect items up to an 11x11x11 area. Opening up the interface allows you to adjust the collector area.",
    "",
    "Upgrading to an &dAdvanced Item Collector&r allows for more control, giving you options for filtering items it collects, as well as extending the collection range to a max of 15x15x15.",
  ],
  "quest.1706D0B9391ED8E1.title": "&fEnergy Cables",
  "quest.1739969280BB4E82.quest_desc": [
    "The &aRedstone Conduit&r carries a signal along the bundle instead of running dust across the floor.",
    "",
    "Signals travel on colored channels, so one bundle can carry several unrelated circuits at once. Set the color on both ends or nothing arrives.",
  ],
  "quest.2CB3974E1A8F41AB.title": "&6Mechanical Power",
  "quest.7427A235CA6E7A6B.title": "&2ComputerCraft: Tweaked",
  "quest.3C0D9DFFEC915E2C.title": "&fFluid Conduit",
  "task.60AE0E54D1CAE9EE.title": "&fBatteries",
  "quest.050A686968533B13.title": "&bCelestine",
  "quest.073CE47053CFE80C.title": "&5Vacuum Pipes",
  "quest.7F4E7C687E7D8707.title": "&eItem Collectors",
  "quest.40255F6F1C60B588.quest_desc": [
    "The fluid versions. &aFluid Interface&r, &2Fluid Exporter&r and Fluid Importer behave exactly like their item counterparts, with tanks in place of inventories.",
    "",
    "Point an importer at a machine that makes a byproduct you keep forgetting to drain, and it stops being a problem you have to remember.",
  ],
  "quest.073CE47053CFE80C.quest_desc": [
    "&aVacuum Pipes&r carry goods around the network.",
    "",
    "The &2Covered Vacuum Pipe&r is the same thing with a camouflage layer, so it takes on the appearance of whatever block you disguise it as and disappears into your build.",
    "",
    "&aImport Chests&r and &2Export Chests&r are the simplest way to get items in and out without configuring anything.",
  ],
  "quest.72AB47828922F73A.title": "&aHarvester Pylon",
  "quest.4D8644BC9308E349.quest_desc": [
    "The item versions of the same three parts. An &aItem Interface&r publishes a chest to the network, an &2Item Exporter&r puts things into a target, an Item Importer takes things out.",
    "",
    "The payoff is that the filter is a variable rather than a slot. One exporter can change what it moves based on what the rest of your base is doing.",
  ],
  "quest.1DAA004E88230E24.title": "&bFilters",
  "quest.163228798680D7ED.title": "&fFluid Card",
  "quest.623C567053E87FA7.title": "&5Going Wireless",
  "quest.7384B838D821EDFC.title": "&2Turtles and Modems",
  "quest.2061FEEF44253E13.quest_desc": [
    "&eLaserIO&r does its work with cards. A &aLaser Node&r on its own moves nothing until you put a card in it and tell the card what to do.",
    "",
    "An &aItem Card&r set to &bExtract&r pulls from the inventory its node touches; set to &bInsert&r it pushes into one. &3Stock&r keeps a target topped up to a set amount, and &bSensor&r emits redstone instead of moving anything.",
    "",
    "Cards run on channels, so several unrelated transfers share one laser without interfering. A &aCard Overclocker&r makes a single card faster.",
  ],
  "quest.79B03C65F6DFCC32.quest_desc": [
    "&eLogistics Networks&r moves items without a single pipe.",
    "",
    "Instead of running a line between two chests, you attach a &aLogistics Node&r directly onto each inventory and put the nodes on the same network from their settings screen. The &aComputer&r is a dashboard on top of that. It lists your networks, shows live throughput and lets you jump to any node's settings.",
    "",
    "No routing, no pathing, no cable to reroute when you rebuild. The nodes just carry the goods.",
    "",
    "&7&oThe Wrench configures a placed node.&r",
  ],
  "quest.5778BAEC8F095B3D.quest_desc": [
    "&eLaserIO&r allows you to transfer pretty much everything using LASERS!",
    "",
    "To get started, you'll need some &aLaser Nodes&r and a &cLaser Wrench&r to connect them. These are the main blocks of the mod, which allows lasers to directly interact with blocks they are attached to.",
    "",
    "To set up how they will interact with the block, you'll need to install &aCards&r to specify what you'd like them to do.",
    "",
    "These cards are highly configurable. For example, &aItem Cards&r can be used to pull or push items from separate inventories, and can be filtered for precise automation.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "When opening up the interface for a &aLaser Node&r, you'll have a tab for every face of the node. This determines the side that the Card works on. Think of the Card as essentially the \"settings file\" for that face.",
    "",
    "The cards can also be upgraded to increase the speed at which it interacts with other blocks, allowing for extremely fast speeds for automation. They can also be filtered and set to specific channels. ",
    "",
    "You're not always going to have straight lasers from each &aLaser Node&r. That's where &aLaser Connectors&r come in!",
  ],
  "quest.4BBEE37F0D847BA9.quest_subtitle": "Transfers Fluids",
  "quest.4E6B5BBF9F8F684A.quest_desc": [
    "&eSFM&r replaces a wall of pipes and filters with a &aprogram&r.",
    "",
    "Put down a &aFactory Manager&r, run Inventory Cable to the inventories you care about, label them with the &2Label Gun&r, then write a short script telling the manager what to move where.",
    "",
    "One manager can do the work of a dozen filtered pipes, and changing it means editing text rather than tearing up a wall.",
    "",
    "&7&oThis quest only gets you started. SFM is deep, and its in-game examples are the best way in.&r",
  ],
  "quest.12662BF53A31F0B4.quest_desc": [
    "Want to keep other players away from your stuff? Make an &aExpulsion Pylon&r!",
    "",
    "This pushes back and prevents players from entering in a set radius around the &aPylon&r. You can also filter out which players are allowed in using &aPlayer Filters&r.",
  ],
  "quest.0ED940DF43A934ED.quest_desc": [
    "The &aVacuum Module&r works exactly like it sounds. This allows the &dRouter&r to collect any item that drops into the world within a certain radius, which can be upgraded by placing &aRange Up Augments&r inside of the module.",
    "",
    "The &aFast Pickup Augment&r can also be placed inside of the module to increase the pickup speed.",
  ],
  "task.62DE6121CE506116.title": "Pipe Upgrades",
  "quest.72AB47828922F73A.quest_desc": [
    "One of the most useful &ePylons&r for managing farms, the &2Harvester Pylon&r allows automatic collection and harvesting of any plants within a configurable radius around it.",
    "",
    "This &aPylon&r works without creating &2item entities&r in the world whenever plants are harvested, and shuts down when the inventory is full or the tool it uses breaks. This makes it great for servers!",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "To use this &aPylon&r, place it in the center of your farm and waterlog it. Open up the interface and place a &aHoe&r inside for it to work with, then adjust the radius you'd like it to cover in the top right. The Hoe you choose to use will take durability each time the pylon collects, so make sure to replace it when needed!",
    "",
    "Once adjusted, you'll want to place an inventory on top of the Pylon for it to output collected items into, and then you are good to go!",
  ],
  "quest.30D0621D928A382A.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click a placed node with the &aWrench&r to open its settings. Each node has 9 channels, and every channel runs in one of two modes.",
    "",
    "- &aSender&r: takes resources out of the block the node is attached to.",
    "- &aReceiver&r: puts resources into the block the node is attached to.",
    "",
    "A Sender only delivers to Receivers on the same channel number, anywhere on the network. A channel number with only Senders or only Receivers on it moves nothing.",
    "",
    "When a Sender can reach several Receivers, its &bDistribution&r setting (Priority, Nearest First, Farthest First or Round Robin) picks the order. &bPriority&r is a number from -99 to 99 that you set on each Receiver. It only counts when the Sender uses Priority distribution, and the highest number is served first.",
  ],
  "quest.4603BA16BDFBE140.title": "&fLong-Range Senders",
  "quest.30D0621D928A382A.title": "&bSenders, Receivers and Priority",
  "task.6ADC311A6F201C21.title": "&dEnder &rCells",
  "task.51876BE373B08431.title": "&dEnder &rGates",
  "task.4723388B7D52CF6E.title": "Any Pipez-Compatible Wrench",
  "quest.2DA8D6D984D83AC5.title": "&fSecurity and Camouflage",
  "quest.571145179B74FD13.title": "&5Nodeworks",
  "quest.2AF7DF42143C5443.quest_desc": [
    "&eIntegrated Dynamics&r is a mod for those who want to bypass the user friendly stuff and get straight into the internals of how things work.",
    "",
    "This is more of an advanced mod, but allows those who master it to take complete control over every aspect of logistics. Near infinite transfer speeds, complete filtering options, you name it.",
    "",
    "Anything can be transferred using &aLogic Cables&r, &2Variable Cards&r, and the appropriate Interface.",
  ],
  "quest.48406B0C45C71D41.title": "&cCables and Bundles",
  "quest.6882C00C9179E7A6.title": "&bNode Upgrades",
  "quest.1F6FE0AAF690665D.title": "&fGeneral Router Upgrades",
  "quest.050A686968533B13.quest_desc": [
    "&eNodeworks&r is a full storage and autocrafting network mod.",
    "",
    "&bCelestine&r is what the whole &eNodeworks&r network is built from, so it comes before anything else in this quest path.",
    "",
    "Find &aDeepslate Celestine Ore&r underground, and look for &3Budding Celestine&r, which grows buds through small, medium and large into a &bCelestine Cluster&r you can harvest repeatedly. Mine Budding Celestine with &bSilk Touch&r to bring it home and grow your own shard supply.",
    "",
    "&7&oSet up a budding farm early. Almost every Nodeworks component wants shards.&r",
  ],
  "quest.7E0E540CF7DB9A40.quest_desc": [
    "The &aPrinting Press&r copies an enchanted book onto a plain Book, and each copy requires special materials.",
    "",
    "Make a &aPrinting Form&r first. To get one, drop an anvil onto the enchanted book you want to copy while it lies on a &2Block of Iron&r or &aBlock of Copper&r. The book and the block are both used up.",
    "",
    "Each copy uses one &aExperience Goop&r, made in the &6FTB Fabricator&r from 4,000 mB of XP Fluid and a &2Vinteum Dust&r once you have killed the Wither.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "An anvil dropped onto enchanted gear lying on a &2Block of Adamantite&r moves each enchantment onto a plain Book from the pile. The block is not used up.",
    "",
    "Enchanted books caught under the anvil are crushed into &aExperience Shards&r. The &6FTB Fabricator&r turns each shard into 250 mB of XP Fluid.",
  ],
  "quest.5FE6AA45E20BD412.quest_desc": [
    "Cards are how a Nodeworks device is told what to do. Write them with the &aCard Programmer&r and slot them in.",
    "",
    "- &aIO Card&r moves things in and out.",
    "- &2Storage Card&r exposes an inventory to the network.",
    "- &aRedstone Card&r ties behavior to a redstone signal.",
    "- &2Observer Card&r watches for changes and reacts.",
    "",
    "&7&oBlank Cards are cheap. Keep a stack around.&r",
  ],
  "quest.6882C00C9179E7A6.quest_desc": [
    "Nodes take tiered upgrades that raise how much they move and how fast they move it.",
    "",
    "- &fIron &f→&6 Gold &r→&b Diamond &r→&7 Netherite",
    "",
    "Work up the ladder as the volume you're shifting grows. A netherite node on a main storage bus is worth several of anything below it.",
  ],
  "quest.7C0EFB4A52F2EC61.title": "&fManaging Power With &ePowah&r!",
  "quest.5CA5F9BE51C24FC8.quest_desc": [
    "A &aRedstone Card&r sends a signal down the same laser your items use.",
    "",
    "Pair it with a card in &bSensor&r mode at the far end and you have a remote switch. One node watches a tank, another shuts a pump off, and nothing runs between them but light.",
  ],
  "quest.1739969280BB4E82.title": "&fRedstone Conduit",
  "task.1F380E6DD3CF799C.title": "General Logistics",
  "quest.57D93B9D1D47057B.title": "&fAugments",
  "quest.57D93B9D1D47057B.quest_desc": [
    "&aAugments&r go inside one module instead of the whole &dRouter&r. Right-click the module in the air to open it, and put them in its augment slots.",
    "",
    "- &aRedstone Augment&r: gives that module its own redstone behavior, separate from the &dRouter&r.",
    "- &aRegulator Augment&r: stops inserting once the target holds a set amount of an item, or stops pulling once the source is down to it.",
    "- &aRange Up Augment&r: adds 1 block of range per augment, up to the module's maximum.",
    "- &aStack Augment&r: lets that one module move several items per operation, overriding the router's &2Stack Upgrades&r.",
  ],
  "quest.745140E3D92CB0D6.quest_desc": [
    "The &aBlock Breaker Module&r allows the &dRouter&r to automatically break blocks adjacent to it and collect any item drops directly into its buffer.",
    "",
    "When crafting the module, enchantments will carry over from the pickaxe used. This can be useful for things like automatic ore processing using &dFortune&r for the module.",
  ],
  "quest.7427A235CA6E7A6B.quest_desc": [
    "&eCC: Tweaked&r puts actual programmable computers in the world, running Lua.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aComputer&r and you get a terminal you can write programs on. Add a &2Disk Drive&r and &aFloppy Disks&r to save and share them, a Monitor to display output, and a Speaker if you want it to make noise about it.",
    "",
    "&7&oIf you have never written a line of code, this mod is a genuinely good place to start.&r",
  ],
  "quest.79B03C65F6DFCC32.title": "&bLogistics Networks",
  "task.33E428135EC63BC7.title": "&fPlayer Transmitters",
  "quest.799515068A0B6D57.quest_desc": [
    "Think of the &aActivator Module&r as the auto-clicker module of &dRouters&r.",
    "",
    "When installed, this module will use the item that is in the router's buffer. This can be configured by right-clicking with the module in the air.",
    "",
    "You can set which direction the item will be used, and even filter which specific items you want used in the top left.",
    "",
    "This is great for certain automation items, like using &2Scythes&r to harvest crops in an area.",
  ],
  "quest.390671750C9DB2AA.title": "&fSync, Muffler and Blast",
  "quest.2A65FC21A4BBF686.quest_desc": [
    "&aEnergy Pipes&r carry power, starting at 256 FE/t and reaching 131,072 FE/t on an &2Ultimate Pipe Upgrade&r.",
    "",
    "Energy has no filters worth setting, so the useful control here is the redstone mode. &bOff When Powered&r turns a pipe line into a switch you can flip from anywhere.",
  ],
  "quest.75C48C2336AC44FE.title": "&fPlayer Module",
  "quest.32DEF2ED50F597AC.title": "&cLogic Gates",
  "quest.1A95C1F8C74D759C.quest_desc": [
    "The &dDimensional Upgrade&r lets a network reach across worlds. It takes spoils from both the Wither and the Ender Dragon, so this one waits for the late game.",
    "",
    "&cIt has to be fitted to both ends.&r A network with nodes in different dimensions won't transfer anything unless the upgrade is on the node at each side, which is the single most common reason one of these setups does nothing.",
  ],
  "quest.7C0EFB4A52F2EC61.quest_desc": [
    "[\"\", {\"text\": \"Powah\", \"color\": \"yellow\"}, \" makes power as well as moving it. Its generators and reactors are covered in the \", {\"text\": \"Powah chapter\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"id\": \"ftbquests:link\", \"payload\": {\"quest_id\": \"659B9311FB49C425\", \"page\": 1}, \"action\": \"custom\"}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Go to the Powah chapter\"}}, \". This part covers moving and storing that power.\"]",
    "",
    "To get started, you'll need some &aDielectric Paste&r to craft the initial components.",
  ],
  "quest.2A65FC21A4BBF686.quest_subtitle": "Transfers Power",
  "quest.55D489754C7B2129.title": "&cMore Red",
  "quest.69C9A63CEDA95037.quest_desc": [
    "Not everything comes out of the network's own crafters. The &aProcessing Handler&r hands a recipe off to an external machine, waits for the result and puts it back into the network.",
    "",
    "&aProcessing Storage&r and &2Processing Sets&r hold the patterns for it, while &bInstruction Crafters&r, &3Instruction Storage&r and &bInstruction Sets&r do the same job for the network's own crafting.",
  ],
  "quest.263A989631CE6F13.title": "&3Keeping Cool",
  "quest.1706D0B9391ED8E1.quest_desc": [
    "&ePowah&r &aEnergy Cables&r transfer FE between generators, batteries and machines. Higher tiers move more energy.",
    "",
    "Their transfer limit comes from the cable tier. Adding more cable blocks does not increase it, and the cables do not store energy as a battery.",
  ],
  "quest.4D21DB3EC7424E9A.quest_desc": [
    "An &aEnergy Card&r moves power between anything two nodes can touch.",
    "",
    "This is where LaserIO earns its place. The laser between two nodes is one connection no matter how far apart they are, so a generator room can feed a base across the map without a cable run.",
  ],
  "quest.1AE69DDE0FBE9E9F.quest_desc": [
    "&aItem Pipes&r move items between inventories with no network to set up. Run a line, then click any pipe with a &aWrench&r to set the direction, the distribution and the filters.",
    "",
    "Bare pipe moves 4 items every 20 ticks. Each upgrade widens that, and an &aUltimate Pipe Upgrade&r gets you 64 items every tick.",
    "",
    "Distribution starts to matter the moment one line feeds two destinations. &bRound Robin&r spreads the load evenly, &bNearest First&r fills the closest inventory before anything else sees an item.",
  ],
  "quest.6BFFC1835C19268A.title": "&5Terminals and Monitors",
  "quest.1AE69DDE0FBE9E9F.quest_subtitle": "Transfers Items",
  "quest.4E6B5BBF9F8F684A.title": "&6Super Factory Manager",
  "quest.390671750C9DB2AA.quest_desc": [
    "Three more upgrades for the &dRouter&r itself.",
    "",
    "- &aSync Upgrade&r: routers whose Sync Upgrades share a tuning value, and that hold the same number of &2Speed Upgrades&r, all run on the same tick. Right-click it to set the value, or Sneak + Right-click for a random one.",
    "- &aMuffler Upgrade&r: one removes sounds, two also remove particles, and three also stop the working animation.",
    "- &aBlast Upgrade&r: makes the &dRouter&r immune to explosions and to bosses that break blocks.",
  ],
  "quest.32DEF2ED50F597AC.quest_desc": [
    "Flat gates that sit on a surface and do one job each:",
    "",
    "AND, OR, NOT, NAND, NOR, XOR, XNOR, plus Diodes, Latches, Pulse Gates and Multiplexers.",
    "",
    "They replace the pile of repeaters and torches you would otherwise need, in a fraction of the space and with no timing surprises.",
    "",
    "&7&oThe Hexidecrubrometer reads a signal's exact strength, which makes debugging a circuit far less of a guessing game.&r",
  ],
  "quest.4348D85E3DB176E2.title": "&fWorking With Power",
  "quest.2AF7DF42143C5443.title": "&eIntegrated Dynamics",
  "quest.2CB3974E1A8F41AB.quest_desc": [
    "The other half of the mod is rotational. &aWindcatchers&r on the roof turn &bAxles&r, &3Gears&r transmit it, and &2Clutches&r and Gearshifters let you start, stop and reverse the drive.",
    "",
    "An &aAlternator&r converts that rotation into a redstone signal, and a &2Stonemill&r puts it to work grinding.",
  ],
  "quest.2061FEEF44253E13.title": "&fItem Card",
  "quest.393850960DC22BB1.quest_desc": [
    "To push and pull items in and out of a &dRouter&r, there are several types of &aModules&r you can install.",
    "",
    "&aSender&r and &2Puller Modules Mk.1&r allow the &dRouter&r to interact with other adjacent inventories.",
    "",
    "To push items wirelessly, you can install &aDistributor Modules&r to distribute items to up to 8 different inventories or blocks within the module's radius.",
    "",
    "To pull items wirelessly, the &aPuller Module Mk.2s&r can be used to pull from a single inventory into the &dRouter&r.",
  ],
  "quest.2A1AE478A678C1A9.quest_desc": [
    "&eIntegrated Tunnels&r turns an &eIntegrated Dynamics&r network into a transfer system. These three parts attach to a cable and do the moving.",
    "",
    "- &aEnergy Interface&r: exposes a machine's power buffer to the network.",
    "- &aEnergy Exporter&r: pushes power from the network into a target.",
    "- &aEnergy Importer&r: pulls power out of a target and into the network.",
    "",
    "None of them act on their own. Each one takes a variable telling it what to move and when, so build the logic first and the transfer second.",
  ],
  "quest.4603BA16BDFBE140.quest_desc": [
    "The &aSender Module Mk2&r sends items to one chosen inventory up to 24 blocks away, with no line of sight needed. &aRange Up Augments&r raise that to 48 blocks.",
    "",
    "Sneak + Right-click an inventory with the module to set its target. Sneak + Right-click any other block to clear it.",
    "",
    "The &dSender Module Mk3&r has no range limit. It sends to any inventory in any dimension, so a &dRouter&r at a far-off farm can feed a chest back at base.",
  ],
  "quest.258F5FED2D319C15.title": "&5Placers, Breakers and Scripts",
  "quest.163228798680D7ED.quest_desc": [
    "Same machinery for tanks, with the same modes and the same channels.",
    "",
    "Mixing item and fluid cards in one node is fine. They only collide if you give them the same channel.",
  ],
  "quest.4D21DB3EC7424E9A.title": "&fEnergy Card",
  "quest.69C9A63CEDA95037.title": "&5Processing",
  "quest.6A4A2A2EFD552316.title": "&fEnergy Cells",
  "quest.094A066E08994C5B.quest_desc": [
    "A &aCrafting Core&r and a touching &2Crafting Buffer&r form the start of a crafting CPU. Connect the core to a Node so the network can use it.",
    "",
    "Add &2Crafting Coolant&r against the buffer before expanding. Buffers and co-processors generate heat, and insufficient cooling slows every craft. A starter buffer can be cooled by two coolant blocks.",
    "",
    "&2Crafting Co-Processors&r add parallel crafts. Coolant blocks become stronger when touching other coolant blocks, but split their cooling between the hot blocks they touch. Keep heat sources spread out and coolant grouped together.",
    "",
    "&2Crafting Substrate&r touching buffers or co-processors increases speed once cooling is covered.",
    "",
    "[\"\", {\"text\": \"Crafting CPU guide\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,nodeworks:guide,nodeworks:items-blocks/crafting_cpu.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Crafting CPU guide\"}}, \" has example layouts and cooling diagrams.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.1739969280BB4E82.quest_subtitle": "Transfers Redstone Signals",
  "quest.4E6EC6E1A507A52B.quest_desc": [
    "&dEnder Gates&r can be placed down on any machine to transfer power wirelessly.",
    "",
    "[\"These will only work if you have enough power in your \", {\"text\": \"Ender Cell\", \"color\": \"dark_purple\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"id\": \"ftbquests:link\", \"payload\": {\"quest_id\": \"1CFBFD1CE648772F\", \"page\": 1}, \"action\": \"custom\"}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Go to Ender Cells Quest\"}}, \" network.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.393850960DC22BB1.title": "&fPushing \\&\\ Pulling",
  "quest.4D8644BC9308E349.title": "&fItem Interfaces",
  "quest.2FCED22162B00429.quest_subtitle": "Transfers Power",
  "quest.48406B0C45C71D41.quest_desc": [
    "&aCables&r come in all sixteen colors and each color carries its own independent signal.",
    "",
    "A &aBundled Cable&r carries all sixteen at once down a single line, which turns a wall of parallel redstone into one cable. &2Cable Junctions&r, &aRelays&r and Redwire Posts route it where you need it.",
    "",
    "&aBitwise&r gates operate on a whole bundle at a time, so you can act on sixteen channels with one component.",
  ],
  "quest.314E9901D4E89E6F.quest_desc": [
    "The &cRedstone Module&r allows the &dRouter&r to give off a redstone signal whenever an item is inside of the buffer slot.",
    "",
    "This can be useful to set up automation, or telling other modules when to activate!",
  ],
  "quest.2FCED22162B00429.quest_desc": [
    "&eEnder IO&r conduits all live in one block. Place a &aConduit Bundle&r and every conduit you add shares the same run, so power, fluid and items follow a single line through your base.",
    "",
    "The &aEnergy Conduit&r comes in tiers, and the tooltip gives you the max output per tick before you commit to a run.",
    "",
    "Hide the whole bundle behind a &aConduit Facade&r once it works. A &aHardened&r facade also survives explosions.",
  ],
  "quest.4BBEE37F0D847BA9.title": "&fFluid Pipe",
  "quest.2FCED22162B00429.title": "&fEnergy Conduit",
  "quest.5FE6AA45E20BD412.title": "&5Cards",
  "quest.6BFFC1835C19268A.quest_desc": [
    "The &aInventory Terminal&r is your window into everything the network is holding, and the &2Portable Inventory Terminal&r is that same window in your pocket.",
    "",
    "The &aMonitor&r shows how much of one item the network holds, so you can see at a glance when something has run dry.",
    "",
    "The &aStorage Meter&r also watches one item, but it acts on it. Right-click it with the item, then set a threshold. It gives off a redstone signal when the stock drops below that number, and with Autocraft on, which is the default, it starts a craft to top the stock back up.",
  ],
  "quest.12662BF53A31F0B4.title": "&fExpulsion Pylon",
  "quest.55D489754C7B2129.quest_desc": [
    "&eMore Red&r is redstone taken seriously. Proper wiring, logic gates and mechanical power, all in flat panels rather than a room full of repeaters.",
    "",
    "It starts with &cRed Alloy&r. Draw it into &cRed Alloy Wire&r, which carries a signal the full length of a run without repeaters and without the mess.",
    "",
    "Red Alloy here is the &aRedstone Alloy Ingot&r. More Red's hand recipe for it is turned off in this pack, so make it in an alloy machine such as the Energized Power &aAlloy Furnace&r.",
    "",
    "&2Pliers&r and the &aSoldering Table&r are the tools you build everything else with.",
  ],
}